Generated keyword lists under syntaxes/ (context-keywords.json and the
inlined repository rules in context.tmLanguage.json) are derived from LMTX
SciTE data tables:

  scite-context-data-context.lua
  scite-context-data-interfaces.lua
  scite-context-data-tex.lua

Typical path under an LMTX install root (context.root):

  tex/texmf-context/context/data/scite/context/lexers/data/

Those tables are part of the ConTeXt distribution (GPL-2). Regenerating them
does not change that: the committed snapshot redistributes derived name lists.

How to refresh
--------------

  CONTEXT_ROOT=/path/to/lmtx npm run generate:keywords

Or from the editor: “ConTeXt: Refresh command keywords” (then reload the window).

Provenance for the committed snapshot is recorded in
syntaxes/context-keywords.json under the "provenance" key (source paths,
SHA-256 hashes, UTC date, and optional LMTX version string).
